/*
 * Composite text-style classes — the full typographic intent of a role in one
 * class, including font-variation-settings, which has no Tailwind utility.
 *
 * Deliberately in `components`, NOT `utilities`: BaseText applies these as role
 * DEFAULTS, the ambient layer under everything else. Typography changes go
 * through BaseText props, which are written inline and so outrank the role
 * class; typography utilities are not a supported override, in DS code or in a
 * consuming app.
 *
 * Nothing here sets line-height: leading is left to inherit, and the consuming
 * app sets it per instance with the lineHeight prop.
 */
@layer components {
  /* .ds-chat-prose (dooph-component-tokens.css) re-spells four of these roles
   * by hand: title (h1), heading (h2), subheading (h3), mono (code). A
   * property added to one of those roles must be added there too. */
